  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wind &amp; Solar to Wheel in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HyGro Energy B.V. is working to realise a green hydrogen chain in the province North Holland. In this chain, green energy is generated by wind energy and then converted into green hydrogen for trucks. Soluforce is the company that supplies the gas pipes. Finally, Milieu Environment B.V./DEBCO, as the initiator of the Dutch Egytium Green Hydrogen Consotirum, is involved in the feasibility study with its local expertise and contacts.The aim of the feasibility study is, on the one hand, to investigate which location within the Suez Canal zone is most suitable, technically and in terms of environmental conditions, to realise the value chain for the production of green hydrogen. On the other hand, based on the selected geographical location, it can be investigated whether this provides a viable business case.In order to conclude this, it is necessary to investigate what the investment will look like in broad terms, how much hydrogen can be produced annually and what the purchase of this hydrogen will look like. The former depends on geographical and climatic conditions and the latter will be benchmarked against alternatives, such as diesel.</narrative>
  </description>
